# FPS_Player.events — first-person player (Task_FPS Phases 1–2).
#
# Scene setup: the player actor carries this sheet's EventSheet with
#   First Person, Use Physics Movement and Move Relative To Camera ticked,
# and a Camera actor is parented under it at eye height
# (that child is the eyes: the mouse pitches it).
#
# The mouse turns the body, so `move forward` walks where you look, and
# `move left`/`right` strafe from the camera without turning it
# (Move Relative To Camera is what guarantees that even if the body ever
# faces somewhere else — aiming does exactly that in Phase 4).
# Feel knobs are globals: `set LookSensitivity to 0.15`,
# `set LookInvertY to 1`.

when game starts
  lock cursor
  set my Pace to 240
  set my RunSpeed to 420
  set my Stamina to 100

when W is held
  Left Shift is held
  my Stamina is higher than 0
  move forward speed my RunSpeed

when W is held
  unless Left Shift is held
  move forward speed my Pace

when S is held
  move backward speed my Pace

when A is held
  move left speed my Pace

when D is held
  move right speed my Pace

# Hold Ctrl to duck. The bridge shortens the capsule, sinks the body (so the
# camera child comes down with it) and halves whatever speed the moves ask for.
when Left Ctrl is pressed
  crouch

when Left Ctrl is released
  stand

when Space is pressed
  jump

# Hand the pointer back so a menu or the debugger stays usable.
when Escape is pressed
  unlock cursor
